---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Shipping Policy | Shandong Shengyuan Peptide"
  description="How Shandong Shengyuan Peptide ships research peptides: cold-chain packaging, international express, tracking, and delivery timelines."
>
  <div class="wrap article-shell">
    <div class="article-header">
      <h1>Shipping Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">How we pack, ship, and track your research peptides worldwide.</p>
    </div>
    <article>
      <h2>Packaging</h2>
      <p>
        Peptides are lyophilized and sealed in sterile vials, then packed with cold-chain protection —
        insulated packaging with temperature buffers where needed — so that products remain stable
        during transit. Each parcel ships with its batch Certificate of Analysis.
      </p>
      <h2>Dispatch Times</h2>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>Stock catalog items</th><td>Ship within 24–48 hours of order confirmation</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Custom synthesis</th><td>Ships after QC release; typically 10–20 business days from kick-off</td></tr>
          <tr><th>OEM programs</th><td>Timeline agreed in the project plan</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <h2>Carriers and Tracking</h2>
      <p>
        We ship through international express networks (FedEx, DHL, UPS, and equivalents) to 50+
        countries. A tracking number is emailed the moment your parcel leaves our facility, and transit
        typically takes 3–7 business days depending on destination.
      </p>
      <h2>Customs</h2>
      <p>
        The buyer is responsible for confirming that the ordered materials may lawfully be imported
        into the destination country and for any duties or clearance requirements. We provide
        documentation support (COA, commercial invoice) with every shipment.
      </p>
      <h2>Damaged or Lost Shipments</h2>
      <p>
        Report any damage within 48 hours of receipt with photographs; we will investigate and arrange
        replacement. Lost shipments are re-sent once the carrier confirms non-delivery.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
